This 1-D problem consists of a porous block sitting between two reservoirs
of high and low pressure air.  This test was created to test the relationship
between momentum exchange coefficients and the mass flow rate.  Other
variables considered included volume fraction of the solid, pressure drop,
length of block and grid resolution.

The "parametricStudies" machinery was used, with some modifications, to run
these tests.  A patch for the src/parametricStudies directory is included here.
There are Instructions for using the parametricStudies tools at:
src/parametricStudies/Instructions.

The results from several tests are included here.  This includes the mass flow
rate data, the gnuplot file used to display it, and a plot showing results.


